This file contains provided code, testers, and test cases.

provided shouls be a top level package in your src directory
JottParserTester and JottTokenizerTester classes should be in a package call testers.

the testCases directories should be in the working directory of your project. 

Setup guide

Ran terminal command:  mkdir -p bin && javac -d bin project_files/provided/*.java project_files/testers/*.java

Ran terminal command:  cd /workspaces/jot_translator/project_files && java -cp ../bin testers.JottTokenizerTester

## Required commands

From the repo root:

```bash
cd /workspaces/jot_translator
mkdir -p bin
javac -d bin project_files/provided/*.java project_files/testers/*.java
```

Then run testers from the directory that contains the test data:

```bash
cd project_files
java -cp ../bin testers.JottTokenizerTester
java -cp ../bin testers.JottParserTester
```

---

## Optional workspace-root fix

If you want to run the testers directly from jot_translator instead of project_files, also update the test case paths in both tester files:

- In JottTokenizerTester.java: change `tokenizerTestCases/...` to `project_files/tokenizerTestCases/...`
- In JottParserTester.java: change `parserTestCases/...` to `project_files/parserTestCases/...`

---

## Notes
- The test runner depends on the working directory, so `cd project_files` is the simplest fix.